---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Cmd from '../../../components/Cmd.astro';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../../lib/release';
---
<Doc
  title="Build from source"
  description="Requirements, commands and tests to build YTS Player (Tauri 2, React and Rust) on Linux and Windows."
  lede="YTS Player is open source. This is how to build it, run it in development mode and run the tests."
>
  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Node 24 and stable Rust.</li>
    <li>On Windows, the Visual Studio Build Tools (C++) with WebView2.</li>
    <li>On Ubuntu or Mint, these system dependencies:</li>
  </ul>
  <Cmd cmd={`sudo apt install libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev build-essential libssl-dev librsvg2-dev libayatana-appindicator3-dev \\
  gstreamer1.0-libav gstreamer1.0-plugins-good gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad`} />

  <h2 id="build">Build</h2>
  <Cmd label="Clone and install dependencies" cmd={`git clone ${REPO_URL}.git
cd yts-movie-player
npm install`} />
  <Cmd label="Development" cmd="npm run tauri dev" />
  <Cmd label="Installer packages" cmd="npm run tauri build" />
  <p>The packages end up in <code>src-tauri/target/release/bundle/</code> (the <code>.exe</code> on Windows).</p>

  <h2 id="tests">Tests</h2>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Command</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Front end (Vitest)</td><td><code>npm test</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rust</td><td><code>cd src-tauri && cargo test</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Interface (Playwright)</td><td><code>npm run ui</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Real app (WebdriverIO)</td><td><code>npm run app</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The E2E tests live in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/e2e`}><code>e2e/</code></a>.</p>

  <h2 id="stack">Stack</h2>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Desktop</td><td>Tauri 2</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Interface</td><td>React 19 + TypeScript, TanStack Router and Query, Tailwind</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Torrent</td><td>librqbit</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Local streaming server</td><td>axum, with <code>Range</code> support</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Data and network</td><td>rusqlite, reqwest</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The project was built in phases by several coordinated AI agents; the details are in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/AGENTS.md`}><code>AGENTS.md</code></a> and <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md`}><code>docs/ROADMAP.md</code></a> (in Spanish).</p>
</Doc>
